iew tape from their investigation  on him she hears a coin a drop as one of  the coin-eyed spirits seen in the  photograph appears in the room behind  her she goes back to the hall where  another coin rolls down the stairs and  lands at her feet she picks it up and  examines it to find several slashes  across the surface as if something very  powerful had scratched at it repeatedly  hard enough to do physical damage the  fairy man continues to roll his precious  coins in her direction sending her on a  path to the source when she reaches the  kitchen an almost insectile hissing  sound directs her attention to the  laundry room  that's when she first lays eyes on  what's at this point has only been a  figure of greek legend to her she locks  eyes with two coins floating near the  ceiling in the dark  [Music]  the positioning of the fairy man  seemingly perched on the ceiling is  something that we've seen before in the  annabelle spin-off movies on multiple  occasions malthus has climbed around on  a ceiling before pouncing down on his  prey for this reason i would assume the  fairy man is seemingly performing the  same ceiling hang trick here is a result  of influence by malthus whether malthus  simply taught him how to do it or took  hold of him in the same fashion we saw  the demon valik take hold of the old man  of bill wilkins in the conjuring 2. in  any event mary ellen is able to defend  herself by shining her flashlight at the  coins causing the fairy man to disappear  and the coins to fall to the ground her  flashlight dies and she picks up one of  the coins to examine it but as she does  so the fairy man rushes forward right in  front of her coins once again cover his  eyes and we get a good look at his dark  dry looking face mary ellen screams and  tries to run for it but she's knocked to  the ground by a supernatural force then  irrigated back into the darkness she's  only able to stop herself by grabbing  onto a door frame for dear life at this  point the